{"itchsRODTEPDtlsDTO":null,"notes":[{"noteId":3.33000283E8,"noteName":"Main","noteDetails":[{"notetype":"Main","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"20","noteSerialNo":"1","notes":"<p>This Chapter does not cover :</p>\n\n<p>(a) vegetables, fruit or nuts, prepared or preserved by the processes specified in Chapter 7, 8 or 11;</p>\n\n<p>(b) vegetable fats and oils (Chapter 15);</p>\n\n<p>(c) food preparations containing more than 20% by weight of sausage, meat, meat offal, blood, insect, fish or crustaceans, molluscs or other aquatic invertebrates, or any combination thereof (Chapter 16);</p>\n\n<p>(d) bakers wares and other products of heading 1905; or</p>\n\n<p>(e) homogenised composite food preparations of heading 2104.</p>\n","notificationNo":"Notification No. 54/2015-2020","notificationDate":"20/01/2009","noteSection":"IV"},{"notetype":"Main","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"20","noteSerialNo":"2","notes":"Headings 2007 and 2008 do not apply to fruit jellies, fruit pastes, sugar-coated almonds or the like in the form of sugar confectionery (heading 1704) or chocolate confectionery (heading 1806).","notificationNo":"","notificationDate":"","noteSection":"IV"},{"notetype":"Main","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"20","noteSerialNo":"3","notes":"Headings 2001, 2004 and 2005 cover, as the case may be, only those products of Chapter 7 or of heading 1105 or 1106 (other than flour, meal and powder of the products of Chapter 8) which have been prepared or preserved by processes other than those referred to in Note 1(a).","notificationNo":"","notificationDate":"","noteSection":"IV"},{"notetype":"Main","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"20","noteSerialNo":"4","notes":"Tomato juice, the dry weight content of which is 7% or more is to be classified in heading 2002.","notificationNo":"","notificationDate":"","noteSection":"IV"},{"notetype":"Main","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"20","noteSerialNo":"5","notes":"For the purposes of heading 2007, the expression \"obtained by cooking\" means obtained by heat treatment at atmospheric pressure or under reduced pressure to increase the viscosity of a product through reduction of water content or other means.","notificationNo":"","notificationDate":"","noteSection":"IV"},{"notetype":"Main","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"20","noteSerialNo":"6","notes":"For the purposes of heading 2009, the expression \"juices, unfermented and not containing added spirit\" means juices of an alcoholic strength by volume (see Note 2 to Chapter 22) not exceeding 0.5% volume.","notificationNo":"","notificationDate":"","noteSection":"IV"}],"noteSectionDetails":[{"notetype":"Main","policyType":"IMPORT","section":"IV","noteSerialNo":"1","notes":"In this Section the term \"pellets\" means products which have been agglomerated either directly bycompression or by the addition of a binder in a proportion not exceeding 3 % by weight.","notificationNo":"","notificationDate":""}]},{"noteId":3.33000284E8,"noteName":"Sub-Heading","noteDetails":[{"notetype":"Sub-Heading","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"20","noteSerialNo":"1","notes":"For the purposes of sub-heading 2005 10, the expression \"homogenised vegetables\" means preparations of vegetables, finely homogenised, put up for retail sale as food suitable for infants or young children or for dietetic purposes, in containers of a net weight content not exceeding 250 g. For the application of this definition no account isto be taken of small quantities of any ingredients which may have been added to the preparation for seasoning, preservation or other purposes. These preparations may contain a small quantity of visible pieces of vegetables. Sub-heading 2005 10 takes precedence over all other sub-headings of heading 2005.","notificationNo":"","notificationDate":"","noteSection":"IV"},{"notetype":"Sub-Heading","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"20","noteSerialNo":"2","notes":"For the purposes of sub-heading 2007 10, the expression \"homogenised preparations\" means preparations of fruit,finely homogenised, put up for retailsale asfood suitable for infants or young children or for dietetic purposes, in containers of a net weight content not exceeding 250 g. For the application of this definition no account is to be taken ofsmall quantities of any ingredients which may have been added to the preparation for seasoning, preservation or other purposes. These preparations may contain a small quantity of visible pieces of fruit. Sub-heading 2007 10 takes precedence over all other Sub-headings of heading 2007.","notificationNo":"","notificationDate":"","noteSection":"IV"},{"notetype":"Sub-Heading","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"20","noteSerialNo":"3","notes":"For the purposes of sub-headings 2009 12, 2009 21, 2009 31, 2009 41, 2009 61 and 2009 71, the expression \"Brix value\" means the direct reading of degrees Brix obtained from a Brix hydrometer or of refractive index expressed in terms of percentage sucrose content obtained from a refractometer, at a temperature of 20°C or corrected for 20°C if the reading is made at a different temperature.","notificationNo":"","notificationDate":"","noteSection":"IV"}],"noteSectionDetails":[]},{"noteId":3.33000285E8,"noteName":"Supplementary Notes","noteDetails":[{"notetype":"Supplementary Notes","policyType":"IMPORT","chapter":"20","noteSerialNo":"1","notes":"<p style=\"text-align:justify\"><span style=\"font-size:12.0pt\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\">For the purposes of tariff items 2008 19 21 to 2008 19 29, the term &ldquo;makhana&rdquo; means the seed of plant Euryale ferox Salisb. and also commonly known as gorgon nut or fox nut.&rsquo;</span></span></p>\n","notificationNo":"44/2025-26","notificationDate":"15/10/2025","noteSection":"IV"}],"noteSectionDetails":[]}],"itcCodeClassifications":[{"itcCodeId":null,"unitOfMeasure":null,"itcCode":"2001","itcDescription":"Vegetables, fruit, nuts and other edible parts of plants, prepared or preserved by vinegar or acetic acid.